--ISSUE
Content-Type: application/issue
ID: 4
Type: feature
Title: configure: soften host prerequisites when --with-docker-gcc is used
Status: in-progress
Priority: medium
Created: 2026-10-05
Relationships: 
Description: When --with-docker-gcc is given, the build runs inside Docker, so
             host-side prerequisites (gcc, make, perl, libelf-dev, libssl-dev,
             etc.) are not required. Change configure.ac so that these checks
             emit warnings instead of hard errors when --with-docker-gcc is
             active. Only docker buildx should remain a hard prerequisite in
             that path.
